flowchart TD
    accTitle: BlaBla agent workflow
    accDescr: An agent starts from the AGENTS.md block and runs blabla status, then blabla explain to recover only the relevant memory and rules. Where a project uses the development loop, the orchestrator opens a bounded task recording write scope and deliverables; a worker implements inside that scope and runs the focused checks that cover the change. blabla challenge then checks the recorded account against deterministic evidence, which is separate from the independent reviewer role that reads the diff and records findings. The orchestrator resolves findings and integrates. Only blabla finish decides project completion, and a challenge does not change its verdict or its exit code.
    agents["AGENTS.md block<br/>Start with: blabla status"]
    status["blabla status<br/>BEHAVIOR · STRUCTURE · OVERALL<br/>memory identities · open tasks"]
    explain["blabla explain &lt;identity&gt;<br/>one rule, system, role or flow"]
    task["blabla task open<br/>write scope · deliverables"]
    implement["worker: implement inside scope<br/>ordinary code, never the contracts"]
    focused["focused checks<br/>only what changed"]
    challenge["blabla challenge<br/>deterministic evidence check<br/>decides no completion"]
    review["reviewer: independent review<br/>reads the task and the diff"]
    findings["blabla task finding<br/>recorded, outlives the context"]
    integrate["orchestrator: resolve and integrate<br/>blabla task resolve"]
    finish["blabla finish<br/>VERIFYING → progress → verdict"]
    red["RED or YELLOW<br/>NOT COMPLETE"]
    green["OVERALL GREEN<br/>the only completion signal"]
    agents --> status --> explain --> task --> implement --> focused --> challenge
    challenge -.unreconciled.-> implement
    challenge --> review --> findings --> integrate --> finish
    finish --> red --> explain
    finish --> green
